description=Realistic, balanced traits, mostly negative, that add complications to work around: Alcoholic, Smoker, Brittle, Arthritis, Caffeine Dependent, Migraines, Hemophilia, Anaemic, Major Depressive Disorder, Hallucinations, Brittle Asthma, Gluten Intolerance, Vegetarian, Diabetes Type 1 and Type 2, Heart Condition, Epilepsy, Multiple Sclerosis, Gout, Essential Tremor, Underactive Thyroid, Hay Fever, Carpal Tunnel, Tinnitus, Lactose Intolerance, Germaphobe, Straight Edge, Homebody, Sweaty, Sensitive Skin, Sensory Issues, ADHD, High Strung, Can't Switch Off, four crippled starts (A Really Bad Day, Wounded, Robbed, Hunted) and five fitness flaws, plus the positive Renaissance Faire Geek, Gym Regular, Early Riser, Meal Prepper, Deep Sleeper, Steady Hands, Night Shift, Hollow Legs, Fast Recovery, Good Clotter, Thick Skull, Grit, Nomad, Cool Customer, Slob, Homemaker, Level Headed, Unwinds Easily, Newbie Gains and five fitness perks, and In Their 20s / 30s / 40s / 50s for the Age system, each decade with traits and small wants of its own. The game's own traits are left alone; Resilient, Iron Gut, Keen Cook, Blacksmith Knowledge, Fear of Blood and Cat's Eyes are re-priced for what this mod adds to them, and Outdoorsman shrugs off sunburn. For everyone: Vitality (fresh food, exercise and sleep slowly earn small stat boosts, junk and neglect the reverse), fitness training (muscle groups that tire and recover, improvised weights, stretching, training plans), cooked meals that lift your mood and fuel training, burnout (fighting wears on you over days and slows what it teaches), sleep and light (and sleeping in your clothes), a home that does you good, laundry (washing floors, damp and musty clothes, stains, clotheslines), reading for pleasure (genres, long reads, tastes, the Good Read moodle, real 1993 books), hangovers and drink relief, sunburn (and sun block to keep it off) and dehydration, a health overhaul (blood loss and shock, wound infection and antibiotics, wound care, what First Aid tells you, a blood readout, a medication reminder, an adrenaline shot, concussion, passing out) and a Guide tab in the character window, most with a sandbox switch. Singleplayer only for now. The moodles need Moodle Framework.
